("`defaultValue` maps to the `value` attribute for initial render; React 19 refines some of these paths ⚠.",
 "`defaultValue` maps to the `value` attribute for initial render. Observable detail (executed in jsdom 2026-10-22 and confirmed in `ReactDOMInput.js` `updateInput`): updating a controlled `<input value>` from `\"a\"` to `\"b\"` produces `attributes` mutation records, not only a property write: React temporarily clears and restores `name` (to keep radio groups atomic) and also mirrors the new value into the `value` *attribute* (\"attribute syncing\"). So a `MutationObserver` on a controlled input is noisy, and \"one write per change\" does not hold for form controls."),
("Similarly, `Activity` (hidden mode ⚠ verify) preserves DOM and state while visually hidden.",
 "Similarly, `<Activity mode=\"hidden\">` (stable since React 19.2) preserves DOM and state while visually hidden (`display: none`). Executed 2026-10-22 on react 19.3.1: with Suspense hiding, only *layout* effects are cleaned up and passive effects stay mounted; with `Activity` hidden, both layout **and passive** effects are cleaned up and re-created on reveal (state preserved, no re-init). Also, per react.dev, text-only children render nothing when hidden because there is no element to hide, and `hideInstance` on a bare text node blanks its `nodeValue`."),
